      <trans-unit id="help.current_pace.what">
        <source>help.current_pace.what</source>
        <target>This card shows how many kilometres you currently drive on average per day, per week and per month.

Polaris takes your whole lease into account, giving more weight to the last 30 days. So if your habits change, the values adjust gradually over the following weeks.</target>
      </trans-unit>
      <trans-unit id="help.current_pace.use">
        <source>help.current_pace.use</source>
        <target>Compare these values with those of the “Budget” card. If your current pace is above your budget, you may exceed your allowance at the end of the lease.</target>
      </trans-unit>
      <trans-unit id="help.budget.answer">
        <source>help.budget.answer</source>
        <target>How many kilometres can you still drive?</target>
      </trans-unit>
      <trans-unit id="help.budget.what">
        <source>help.budget.what</source>
        <target>This card shows how many kilometres you can drive on average per day, per week and per month to use exactly your allowance by the end of the lease.

The calculation takes into account the kilometres you have left and the time remaining until the end of your contract.</target>
      </trans-unit>
      <trans-unit id="help.budget.use">
        <source>help.budget.use</source>
        <target>Your budget goes up when you drive less and down when you drive more.

By keeping your driving pace below these values, you avoid exceeding your allowance and paying for extra kilometres.</target>
      </trans-unit>
      <trans-unit id="help.even_pace.answer">
        <source>help.even_pace.answer</source>
        <target>Your allowance, spread evenly.</target>
      </trans-unit>
      <trans-unit id="help.even_pace.what">
        <source>help.even_pace.what</source>
        <target>This card shows the average number of kilometres your contract allows you to drive per day, per week and per month over the whole lease.

These values are fixed and do not change with how you actually use the vehicle.</target>
      </trans-unit>
      <trans-unit id="help.even_pace.use">
        <source>help.even_pace.use</source>
        <target>Use this card as a reference to compare your current driving pace and your remaining budget.</target>
      </trans-unit>
