        <target>You drove fewer kilometres than your budget allowed.</target>
      </trans-unit>
      <trans-unit id="help.compare_budget.reference">
        <source>help.compare_budget.reference</source>
        <target>Your budget is the number of kilometres you can drive each day to reach exactly your allowance at the end of the lease. Polaris uses the budget calculated at the start of the period, recorded every day at midnight.</target>
      </trans-unit>
      <trans-unit id="help.compare_budget.percent">
        <source>help.compare_budget.percent</source>
        <target>The percentage shows the gap between the two values, relative to the distance your budget allowed. It only appears once 6 hours of the period have passed, to avoid swings that are too large.</target>
      </trans-unit>
      <trans-unit id="help.compare_pace.answer">
        <source>help.compare_pace.answer</source>
        <target>Are you driving more or less than usual?</target>
      </trans-unit>
      <trans-unit id="help.compare_pace.actual">
        <source>help.compare_pace.actual</source>
        <target>Distance actually driven</target>
      </trans-unit>
      <trans-unit id="help.compare_pace.expected">
        <source>help.compare_pace.expected</source>
        <target>Distance estimated from your usual pace</target>
      </trans-unit>
      <trans-unit id="help.compare_pace.over">
        <source>help.compare_pace.over</source>
        <target>You drove more kilometres than usual.</target>
      </trans-unit>
      <trans-unit id="help.compare_pace.under">
        <source>help.compare_pace.under</source>
        <target>You drove fewer kilometres than usual.</target>
      </trans-unit>
      <trans-unit id="help.compare_pace.reference">
        <source>help.compare_pace.reference</source>
        <target>Your usual pace is your average number of kilometres driven per day since the start of the lease. The last 30 days weigh more in this calculation so that it better reflects your recent habits.

Polaris records this average every day at midnight. If no data is available for the first day of a period, the row says “Not enough history”.</target>
      </trans-unit>
      <trans-unit id="help.compare_pace.percent">
        <source>help.compare_pace.percent</source>
        <target>The percentage shows the gap between the two values, relative to your usual pace. It only appears once 6 hours of the period have passed, to avoid swings that are too large.</target>
      </trans-unit>
      <trans-unit id="help.compare_projected_end.answer">
